      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The delivery system utilizes nucleoside-modified mRNA encapsulated within lipid nanoparticles (LNPs), engineered with optimized ionizable cationic lipids achieving superior endosomal escape via protonation-driven membrane destabilization. This formulation significantly enhances translational efficiency while mitigating innate immune responses by evading TLR7/8 sensing pathways. In murine subjects, subcutaneous LNP administration yielded a 15-fold upregulation in target protein expression relative to control PEGylated systems, concurrently demonstrating reduced systemic pro-inflammatory cytokine release, notably IL-6 and TNF-α.",
      "source": "target",
